      "title": "OpenSSL: Buffer overflow in EVP_EncodeBlock() (CVE-2026-121481, CVSS 9.8)",
      "url": "https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33652",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50569226",
      "score": 364,
      "comments": 328,
      "author": "JacobHenner",
      "published": "2026-11-20T02:01:09Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Critical CVSS 9.8 buffer overflow in OpenSSL's EVP_EncodeBlock() base64 encoding function poses severe arbitrary memory corruption and RCE risks.",
        "The flaw typically stems from improper output buffer length calculations, exposing network services accepting user-controlled data to unauthenticated attacks.",
        "Prioritize patching OpenSSL across TLS proxies, custom application builds, and container images to remediate CVE-2026-121481 immediately."
      ]
    },
